{"actor_ref":"claude","class":"draft_history","document_uuid":"01a1a54a-31d8-7090-87f4-34945f6076a2","id":"01a1a65d-906f-761c-bfa8-9fa274395db8","idempotency_key":"393ba6cd9f242d9be547cac2b8584524cf2e01403b690dff48da34b991bbfdc7","occurred_at":"2026-11-04T11:41:52Z","payload":{"note":"5 of 5, closed. The middle column embeds the board now: the active board, its move list as a clickable tree (each SAN jumps the board to that ply), arrows and circles rendered as shapes from the board's content, and the comments recorded against plies. The last check found a real UI bug rather than a test bug: clicking a chapter set the chapter and the notes but never reloaded the board, so the tree and the position described the chapter you had left. Selecting a chapter now selects its first board, and a tick signal re-runs the board effect when a reload brings a new revision of a board whose id has not changed - watching the id alone missed exactly that. cdp_study.js now seeds a board with two moves, an arrow and a comment, reloads the chapter and asserts the tree shows e4 e5 and the comment renders: AI_STUDY_PASS. Reminder of what this ticket did NOT settle: the frontend crate still carries a ~39-lint backlog that predates this work, and i-c9a0's arrows are rendered but not editable in the study column - editing shapes happens in Analysis.","target":"t-5638"},"type":"work.note_added","v":2}
